%% Operating modes, with the trigger and the component that owns each transition.
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Normal
    Normal --> PreOutage: C7 — DISCOM load-shedding notice
    PreOutage --> Normal: C7 — notice withdrawn
    PreOutage --> Backup: C9 — grid lost at the cut
    Normal --> Backup: C9 — unplanned fault (all sensors dark)
    Backup --> Restoration: C9 — grid returns
    Restoration --> Normal: C9 → C7 — staggered re-transfer complete
    Normal: Normal (C7)
    Normal: shave evening peak, charge midday, DR on stress days
    PreOutage: Pre-outage (C7)
    PreOutage: reserve = backup need ×1.5, keep shaving with the rest
    Backup: Backup (C9)
    Backup: inverters islanded on the backup circuit only, premises by priority
    Restoration: Restoration (C9)
    Restoration: batched re-transfer to avoid cold-load pickup
